From 0a72c848508eb08823b42710cff5931260049baf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:43:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] arrange: make the pretest's "filtered:" label a
 statement

The label in TRY_CHILD was followed by a declaration (const int cross),
which only C23 allows; GCC accepts it as an extension and warns under
-std=c17 -pedantic, and older or stricter compilers reject it. An empty
statement after the label keeps the code the same in every standard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
---
 src/c/arrange_core.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/c/arrange_core.h b/src/c/arrange_core.h
index 6408e2a..113ea9b 100644
--- a/src/c/arrange_core.h
+++ b/src/c/arrange_core.h
@@ -1237,7 +1237,7 @@ static inline TRY_CHILD_INLINE void TRY_CHILD(sstate_t *s, int d, int b,
       for (int w = 0; w < W; w++)
         dead |= ncell_o[w] & ~ncell_b[w] & ~ub[w];
     CP_WHY(CD_FC_B);
-  filtered:
+  filtered:; /* (a label must precede a statement before C23) */
     /* with two rows and two cols placed, most children are dead, and cross
      * support (with the support filter's test folded in) finds it faster
      * than the support filter's cascade: on the o candidates first, which
